      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve for \\(a\\) in the function \\(g(x) = 3x - 4\\) where \\(g(a) = 0\\), we need to set the function equal to zero and solve for \\(a\\).\n\nStarting with the equation:\n\\[ g(a) = 0 \\]\n\nSubstitute \\(g(x)\\) with \\(3x - 4\\):\n\\[ 3a - 4 = 0 \\]\n\nNext, isolate \\(a\\) by adding 4 to both sides of the equation:\n\\[ 3a - 4 + 4 = 0 + 4 \\]\n\\[ 3a = 4 \\]\n\nNow, divide both sides by 3 to solve for \\(a\\):\n\\[ \\frac{3a}{3} = \\frac{4}{3} \\]\n\\[ a = \\frac{4}{3} \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(a\\) that satisfies \\(g(a) = 0\\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{4}{3}} \\]",
