      "text": "To find the value of \\(a\\) for which \\(g(a) = 0\\), we start by substituting \\(a\\) into the function \\(g(x) = 3x - 4\\). This gives us the equation:\n\n\\[\ng(a) = 3a - 4\n\\]\n\nWe are given that \\(g(a) = 0\\). Therefore, we can set up the equation:\n\n\\[\n3a - 4 = 0\n\\]\n\nNext, we solve for \\(a\\) by isolating it on one side of the equation. We do this by adding 4 to both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[\n3a - 4 + 4 = 0 + 4\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n3a = 4\n\\]\n\nNow, we divide both sides by 3:\n\n\\[\na = \\frac{4}{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(a\\) for which \\(g(a) = 0\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{4}{3}}\\).",
